From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the shell may cast the desktop to a TV

The shell lists the TVs Chrome's Media Router finds and casts the
desktop to them. Its browser side binds CastSinks for the shell's
document only, as BrowserWindows does: a page that could reach it could
put the desktop on any TV in the house. Blink builds the TV interface
that `domicile.castSinks` lists.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 .../browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc  | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 .../renderer/bindings/generated_in_modules.gni   |  2 ++
 .../blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_modules.gni   |  1 +
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
index abc0016..8a5a575 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "base/task/bind_post_task.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_extension_installer.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_browser_windows.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_cast_sinks.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_extension_tray.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_pointer_warp.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_shell_fetch.h"
@@ -656,6 +657,21 @@ void PopulateChromeFrameBinders(
         domicile::BindBrowserWindows(frame, std::move(receiver));
       }));
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork: the TVs to cast the desktop to, for the shell.
+  //
+  // Gated at BIND time like the browser windows: a page that could reach this
+  // could put the desktop on any TV in the house.
+  map->Add<domicile::mojom::CastSinks>(base::BindRepeating(
+      [](content::RenderFrameHost* frame,
+         mojo::PendingReceiver<domicile::mojom::CastSinks> receiver) {
+        if (!domicile::IsShellOrigin(frame->GetLastCommittedOrigin())) {
+          mojo::ReportBadMessage(
+              "domicile: only the shell may cast the desktop.");
+          return;
+        }
+        domicile::BindCastSinks(frame, std::move(receiver));
+      }));
+
   // Domicile's engine fork: GETs with the profile's cookies, for the shell.
   //
   // Gated at BIND time like the browser windows, and for their reason: a page
